# Close the last gap to a measured object, after navigation has got the robot roughly there.
#
# Exists because navigation cannot hand manipulation a pose it can work with: Nav2's
# xy_goal_tolerance is 0.5 m and the arm's whole reach envelope is about 0.13 m wide.
#
# This does NOT converge on a distance setpoint. The gait's smallest forward pulse measures
# 0.3 to 0.6 m -- larger than the reach tolerance -- so no control law can hit a 5 cm target
# head-on. It walks in pulses, re-reads the object between each one, and approaches obliquely
# once the remaining distance is under one pulse, so the advance per pulse is what shrinks
# rather than the step. See docs/notes/m9-base-approach.md.

# Must match a class_id published on /objects. The pose is read fresh from there rather than
# passed in, for the same reason Pick does it: a retry re-reads instead of replaying.
string object_id
# Which arm has to reach it. Only selects which side of the pelvis the object should end up on;
# nothing here moves an arm.
string ARM_LEFT=left
string ARM_RIGHT=right
string arm
# Give up after this many seconds. 0 uses the server's own default.
float64 timeout_s
---
bool success
# On failure, names the phase that failed and why. Not meant to be parsed.
string message
# Where the object ended up relative to the base, so a caller can see how close it got rather
# than only whether it succeeded.
float64 final_range_m
float64 final_bearing_rad
---
# Which phase is running. Also what the result message names on failure, so the constants live
# here rather than as literals in the server and its tests.
string PHASE_LOCATING=locating
string PHASE_FACING=facing
string PHASE_CLOSING=closing
string PHASE_VERIFYING=verifying
string phase
float64 range_m
float64 bearing_rad
int32 pulses
